# Issue #40 chunk 3 paired benchmarks — all three subchunks did NOT meet gate
#
# Per-subchunk plan and reference:
#   https://github.com/imazen/jxl-encoder/issues/40#issuecomment-4466097630
#
# BASELINE for all three subchunks: jj commit e3cea6f0 (= chunk-2 landed at
# f5ea70f, plus only-docs change c82e05c). Tip of jxl-encoder/main on
# 2026-05-16, with the SplittableSamples in-place permutation wired into
# `find_best_split`.
#
# Profile images (same 3 as chunks 1-2):
#   7256805.png                                   512x512   0.26 MP (CID22)
#   02809272...cd804f7.png                        1024x1024 1.05 MP (CLIC2025 1024)
#   8426ed22...05ac41.png                         2048x2048 4.19 MP (CLIC2025 final-test)
#
# Pattern (CLAUDE.md): paired interleaved A/B per sample, 5 samples per take,
# 2 takes (10 samples per cell total). CLIFF_THREADS=1, CLIFF_SAMPLES=1 (so
# the cliff harness writes 1 timing per invocation), no `-C target-cpu=native`.
#
# Hardware: AMD Ryzen 9 7950X (water-cooled), Linux 6.6 WSL2.
# System load during measurement: ~10-12 (high — same as chunk 2's "load ~9").
#
# Gate (from user's standing rules for chunk 3):
#   >= 5% wall-clock improvement on >= 2 of 3 profile images.
#
# All three subchunks (3a, 3b, 3c) fall below the gate. None shipped.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Subchunk 3a: Hoist per-pred slice setup outside property loop
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Files: chunk3a_paired_2026-05-16_take{1,2}.csv
#
# Implementation: cache `&samples.residual_tokens[pred][start..end]`,
# `&samples.extra_bits[pred][start..end]`, and the predictor change-penalty
# in a per-call array indexed by `pred`, computed once before the property
# loop. Removes ~num_props × num_pred redundant slice operations + penalty
# arithmetic per `find_best_split` invocation.
#
# Hash locks: 36/36 byte-identical (verified).
#
# Combined 10-sample paired medians:
#   0.26 MP    e7   -2.79%  (no win — below 5% gate)
#   1.05 MP    e7   -0.63%  (essentially noise)
#   4.19 MP    e7   +1.77%  (essentially noise; mean -0.00%)
#
# Hypothesis (post-mortem): LLVM's LICM already hoists trivially loop-
# invariant slices on its own, and the penalty arithmetic is only ~224 f64
# ops per node — under a microsecond out of seconds of work. The manual
# hoist saves the same work the compiler was already doing.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Subchunk 3b: Fused clear+fill+right-init pass (was "block-fold Strategy A2")
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Files: chunk3b_paired_2026-05-16_take{1,2}.csv
#
# Implementation: fuse the three separate traversals of count_increase
# (clear → fill from sorted_by_bucket → sum into right_counts) into a single
# per-bucket inner loop that clears, fills, and folds into right_counts in
# one pass — keeping each bucket row hot in L1 across all three operations.
#
# Note: this is a different shape from the literal "block-fold Strategy A2"
# in the chunk-2 agent's note (which would eliminate counting sort entirely
# and process samples in cache-line blocks). A2-without-counting-sort was
# already shown to regress; the fused-pass variant here preserves counting
# sort but reduces count_increase traversals from 3 to ~1.5.
#
# Hash locks: 36/36 byte-identical (verified).
#
# Combined 10-sample paired medians:
#   0.26 MP    e7   -1.56%  (median;  mean -4.06% — below 5% gate)
#   1.05 MP    e7   -0.63%  (median;  mean -2.12% — below 5% gate)
#   4.19 MP    e7   +2.45%  (median;  mean -0.06% — noise)
#
# Hypothesis (post-mortem): the chunk-2 layout already keeps each bucket's
# count_increase row hot during fill (same bucket → same cache line until
# bucket boundary). The 3-pass structure was a theoretical concern only —
# the data was still hot when the right-init pass arrived. Savings exist
# but are too small to clear the gate.
#
# Note: not the literal block-fold-A2 variant from the chunk-2 agent's
# plan. The aggressive variant (eliminate counting sort, process in cache-
# line blocks, track touched buckets) is materially more complex and the
# agent's own note marked it "May or may not work — measure and document."
# Time-budgeting moved on to subchunk 3c without that experiment.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Subchunk 3c: Skip props i32 swap during partition on lossless main path
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Files: chunk3c_paired_2026-05-16_take{1,2}.csv
#
# Implementation: added `skip_props_swap: bool` to `SplittableSamples`.
# `compute_best_tree_with_budget` (lossless main path) consumes
# `samples.props` once in `pre_quantize` and never reads it again — the
# tree builder only touches `pq.bucket_indices`. Skip the per-property
# Vec<i32> swaps (16+ Vec swaps per row swap) on this path. The
# `compute_best_tree_with_multipliers` path still swaps props because its
# static-prop axes use `PartitionKey::Property` which reads `props[i]` to
# evaluate the predicate.
#
# Hash locks: 36/36 byte-identical (verified).
#
# Combined 10-sample paired medians:
#   0.26 MP    e7   -1.34%  (median;  mean -3.08% — below 5% gate)
#   1.05 MP    e7   -1.96%  (median;  mean -3.03% — below 5% gate)
#   4.19 MP    e7   -0.91%  (median;  mean +7.71% — driven by 34s outlier)
#
# Paired diff analysis (per-sample NEW vs BASELINE):
#   0.26 MP: 10/10 paired wins, median -0.83%, mean -2.78%
#   1.05 MP: 10/10 paired wins, median -1.79%, mean -2.93%
#   4.19 MP: 6/10 paired wins, median -1.84%, mean +8.88% (one 34s outlier
#            in take 2 sample 3; without it, mean ~-2%)
#
# Hypothesis (post-mortem): partition is not the bottleneck. The chunk-2
# agent's pre-estimate ("<2% wall-clock — partition is not the bottleneck
# per chunk-1 microbench's amortization math") proved accurate. The change
# is clean (10/10 paired wins on small + medium, byte-identical output),
# but the magnitude is below the 5% gate.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Conclusion
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# None of the three subchunks reached the 5% × 2 of 3 wall-clock gate.
# Cumulative paired improvement on the medium image (1.05 MP) summed
# across 3a + 3b + 3c is ~5-6% — below the 15% "worth shipping" threshold
# the user's instructions sketched. All three reverted.
#
# The chunk-2 agent's prediction has been confirmed: the architectural
# ceiling on `find_best_split` micro-ops is ~20-30%; we are now ~5% above
# the wall-clock floor those micro-ops can reach. The remaining 2-3x gap
# to libjxl is elsewhere — likely `pre_quantize`, `dedup_samples`,
# `gather_samples`, or the per-pred entropy estimator itself.
#
# Updated CBT vs cjxl gap: unchanged at ~3.5× (per chunk-2's measurement).
